From 46d310d72abed1dabc5526bf7580f2c83aa31bf9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <anthropic@solutious.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 02:47:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add ots_shared/upcloud provider helpers (UpCloud support)

New ots_shared.upcloud package mirroring ots_shared.hcloud, backing the
UpCloud provider in lots:
- config: UPCLOUD_TOKEN (Bearer) | UPCLOUD_USERNAME+PASSWORD (Basic) auth
- errors: api_errors() mapping UpCloudAPIError/ClientError + bounded
  with_backoff/is_retryable for 429/5xx (the SDK has no retry)
- zones: atomic UpCloud zones (region == zone; no network_zone)
- wait: wait_for_state polling (the API has no async action ids)
- server_defaults: MARKER_HOST_FIELDS (region, honored private_ip_*,
  no user_data size cap)
- network_plan: single-range SDN reconciliation (one ip_network/network)

Targets the official upcloud-api 2.9.0 SDK (added as a base dep); every
SDK call site verified against the installed SDK surface.

Tests: tests/upcloud (config/errors/zones/wait/server_defaults/
network_plan) incl. backoff invocation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WjuXAY8vDVWsxk1pjwmhRx
